"{\"advisories\":[{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0182\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24738-security-advisory-0182\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"The VeloCloud Edge software update workflow may accept update bundles without properly validating their signatures because the workflow does not restrict the digest algorithm used for artifact verification. An attacker with either sufficient privileges to upload packages to VeloCloud Orchestrator or credentials permitting direct access to an Edge may be able to install unauthorized software.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0181\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24737-security-advisory-0181\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Insufficient validation of inputs supplied through affected VeloCloud Edge management and configuration workflows may allow an authorized management request or configuration value to be interpreted as an operating-system command. Successful exploitation may allow command execution with elevated privileges on the affected VeloCloud Edge.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0180\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24736-security-advisory-0180\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"The VeloCloud Edge and Gateway exhibit an out-of-bounds write vulnerability when processing tunneled IP fragments between authenticated overlay neighbors. This vulnerability impacts the VeloCloud VCMP tunnel protocol only.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0179\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24735-security-advisory-0179\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"On a VeloCloud Edge, an unauthenticated actor with network access to the private HA (High Availability) interconnect may trigger sensitive HA peer functions without verification.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0178\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24734-security-advisory-0178\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"SNMPv3 credentials may appear in clear text in logs or running config, enabling unauthorized SNMP access.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0177\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24733-security-advisory-0177\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Malformed packets can cause the S4Sync agent to crash, leading to DoS for MLAG synchronization.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0176\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24732-security-advisory-0176\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Misconfigured uRPF allows spoofed-source traffic to bypass the check and traverse the device.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0175\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24731-security-advisory-0175\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"A specially crafted packet can cause the premature expiry of multicast forwarding state on affected interfaces.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0174\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24730-security-advisory-0174\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Unauthenticated attacker can send crafted requests to execute arbitrary code, leading to full device compromise.\"},{\"title\":\"Security Advisory 0173\",\"url\":\"https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24729-security-advisory-0173\",\"date\":\"September 9, 2026\",\"summary\":\"Crafted packets can cause the OSPFv3 agent to restart, causing DoS for IPv6 routing.\"}],\"maxStart\":180}"